  "study": "Post-hoc counterfactual replays on actual L2-L5 content/structure calls, with a common L5 downstream. Each policy is applied to exactly the same accepted content and source on both sides. Standard follows the historical reference size, geometry, fidelity and unchanged exit checks, with the model tree's own order. Compatible keeps a successful legacy program layout, then applies the locked enhanced fallback. A confirmed-pass table counts positive evidence; nonconfirmation may include an unknown verdict. A missing physical model structure is displayed separately and never credited as a program victory. Multiple draws share tasks, sometimes exact content. These are paired technical projections, without visual or business assessments.",
